Here are a few simple fragments to help you.

To check whether a drive or a directory exists, you can try opening its 
root directory, i.e.  ispath%:("LOC::B:\").  You can use this to check
whether any path exists:

PROC ispath%:(cp$)
        LOCAL h%,pp$(128)
        pp$=cp$+"*.*"
        IF IOOPEN(h%,pp$,$30)   REM open directory call
                RETURN 0        REM directory does not exist
        ELSE
                IOCLOSE(h%)     REM it does exist, so close it
                RETURN -1
        ENDIF
ENDP

To check what's in a slot, and its size, etc. (You may be able to use 
this to check the existence of a device instead of ispath%:(), as 
PEEKW(a%), med%, and bt& will all return zero):

PROC free:(device$)
        LOCAL a%,bf&,bt&,med%,n$(8),f%(32),r$(40)
        n$=device$
        a%=ADDR(f%())
        CALL($0a87,UADD(ADDR(n$),1),a%)
        med%=PEEKB(a%+2)
        r$=media$:(med%)    REM  r$ = media type
        bt&=PEEKL(a%+6)     REM  bt& = total bytes on device
        bf&=PEEKL(a%+10)    REM  bf& = free space on device
        REM the 32 bytes from a%+14 hold the volume name
        REM PEEKB(a%+46) should hold 1 if device battery is OK
        REM or zero if battery low, or -4 if battery status n/a
ENDP

PROC media$:(n%)
        IF n%=0 :RETURN "Missing or not known"
        ELSEIF n%=1 :RETURN "Floppy"
        ELSEIF n%=2 :RETURN "Hard Disk"
        ELSEIF n%=3 :RETURN "Flash"
        ELSEIF n%=4 :RETURN "RAM"
        ELSEIF n%=5 :RETURN "ROM"
        ELSEIF n%=6 :RETURN "Write Protected"
        ENDIF
ENDP

All this and much more is in the PSIONICS file SYSCALLS.

Roger


